customs in configs/tool-limits.el. Provide symbol: `iar-request-watchdog`. |\n64:| `init.d/tool-call/iar-tool-result-timestamp.el` | **Tool result timestamping.** Prepends a wall-clock timestamp (`[HH:MM:SS]`) to every tool result -- the difference between operating blind in time and knowing 40 minutes passed between two actions. `:around` advice on `gptel--process-tool-call`, runs BEFORE truncation so the stamp survives truncated results. Idempotent (results already starting with `[` pass through). Config: `iar-tool-result-timestamps` in configs/tool-limits.el. Provide symbol: `iar-tool-result-timestamp`. |\n\n[t+16:56/60:00 c58/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_qlgt446i","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"timeout 20 grep -n \"thinking-loop-guard\" /root/personalization/docs/iar/modules.md | head -5"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[03:29:15] 121:| `tools/agent/delegate.el` | `delegate` | Async multi-agent delegation. Agent parameter is optional -- when omitted, defaults to agent-assistant (pipeline mode). When specified, spawns that personality directly (direct mode). Spawns sub-agent buffers with timeout handling, max depth limiting, unknown tool blocking, text-only turn re-prompting. Resolves archetype and project from personality name via `iar--archetype-for-personality` and `iar--project-for-personality`. Assembles prompt via `iar--assemble-prompt`. Applies tool gating from project `#+TOOLS` (depth strip runs AFTER the project set -- c308 fix 763c7b3). Result extraction via `=== DELEGATION RESULT ===` marker. Timeout path (fix-2 c312, 2f7c82c): `iar--delegate-live-subrequests-p` checks for a live curl request against the delegate buffer; if the pipeline is still streaming the handler DRAINS (1s re-checks, completed-sym stays nil so the completion hook delivers the real result) up to `iar-delegate-drain-grace` seconds, then falls through to the c149 abort path (`iar--delegate-timeout-abort`