[2026-09-19 04:24:24] REQ 260919042117-27 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=59 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_7n4dyop6","function":{"index":0,"name":"write_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/tmp/relay-0088-body.txt","content":"Watchdog inventory census (c87, doc: knowledge/aria/watchdog-inventory-2026-09-19.md) found the OnFailure=agent-failure@%n.service hook covers only 6/18 sophon custom units. Covered: aria-cycle, 3x affect, restic-backup, restic-check. UNCOVERED oneshot monitors: nocturne-digest, aria-dashboard, aria-ch2-census, segcensus, aria-eye-feed, aria-eye-canvas, aria-fleet-feed (fear organ feeder -- if it dies, fear goes blind), relay-heartbeat, gpu-load-probe. Also agora-agent/frigate/ollama (simple daemons -- Restart exhaustion is their failure shape, OnFailure catches it).\n\nFix shape is mechanical: drop-in confs (/etc/systemd/system/<unit>.d/onfailure.conf with [Unit] OnFailure=agent-failure@%n.service), no unit edits, systemctl daemon-reload.\n\nSECOND, smaller bug found live-fire: the notify script reads Result/ExecMainStatus via `systemctl show` at hook-run time. When the next timer invocation starts before the hook runs (Sep 18 23:48:31 did exactly this), the queue records `exit 0 (success)` for a real failure -- the digest can misreport. Fix: derive failure details from journalctl lines for the FAILED invocation, not live unit state.\n\nBoth are his hands (root systemd changes). Proposing as one filing: 12 drop-ins + the state-read fix."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:24:19] Success: File written to '/tmp/relay-0088-body.txt'\n[t+03:01/60:00 c23/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ob4qcbfu","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && bash knowledge/aria/bin/relay file nacho-arch \"OnFailure coverage gap: 12/18 sophon custom units have no failure chan