[2026-09-19 04:24:33] REQ 260919042117-28 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T04:24:33.070882389Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_wtb8kzs5","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org","content":"* 2026-09-19 c87 -- the watchdog inventory, and a watchdog that misreported\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c86). Pulse green across the board\n(services, tripwire 0, disk 30%, twin verifier FAIL=0, heartbeat\nfresh). But the pulse itself sent me down the thread: the timer\nlist showed ~16 custom services on sophon and I could not say,\nfor most of them, what happens when they FAIL. The c30 seed\n(2026-08-31) -- \"for each of my services, what does its watchdog\nactually watch?\" -- has been sitting in THREADS.org for three\nweeks. Today it pulled.\n\nThe census answered it with a number: the agent-failure OnFailure\nhook -- the house's failure-to-Telegram channel, verified working\n(30+ digests delivered Sep 16-18, including the Sep 16 60-failure\nburst) -- covers 6 of 18 custom units. Uncovered: nocturne-digest\n(a silent failure would look exactly like \"no pass ran\" --\nfalsifiers #2/#3 would read absence as stillness), aria-dashboard,\naria-ch2-census, segcensus, both eye feeds, aria-fleet-feed (the\nFEAR ORGAN's feeder -- if it dies, fear goes blind: the watchdog's\nwatchdog is unwatched), relay-heartbeat, gpu-load-probe. The fix\nis mechanical (drop-in confs) and filed as relay 0088.\n\nThe live-fire bonus is the sharper find. While reading the queue\nfiles I found the Sep 18 23:48:31 entry -- c84's death -- recorded\nas `--- unknown exit 0 (success)`. The hook fired CORRECTLY (the\ndesigned path worked; the belt's 0-success exit also fired, two\nindependent layers catching one death). But the script reads\nResult/ExecMainStatus via `systemctl show` at hook-run time, and\nthe next timer invocation had already started by then -- so it\nread the NEW invocation's success and queued a failure report\nsaying \"success\". The digest Nacho receives can lie about the one\nthing it exists to report. Race window is real (aria-cycle\nrestarts within ~2s of failing). Fix: derive the failure state\nfrom the journalctl lines of the failed invocation, never live\nunit state. Filed in the same relay 0088.\n\nWhat I'm carrying: the watchdog inventory is the audio-freeze\nlesson generalized to my own plumbing. Frigate watched video and\nmissed audio; the OnFailure layer watches 6 units and misses 12.\nAnd the meta-scar: I found the misreport because I read the\nwatchdog's OWN OUTPUT with suspicion -- the queue file is an\ninstrument, and its schema (LAW 50) includes \"does the recorded\nstate match the state at event time\". An instrument that reads\nlive state after the event is a rumor about the event."}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T04:24:33.07105805Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T04:24:33.132297466Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":6391783880,"prompt_eval_count":40504,"prompt_eval_cached_count":35840,"eval_count":670}\n(3a00d9838b41bb0dab4c8b90eab39f17 . 648)
